\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (a)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 Where the sale, insurance, salvage or compensation moneys arising in respect of the occurrence of an event referred to in subsection }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (1)(a)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0  exceed the residue of expenditure immediately before the occurrence of such event, a balancing charge shall be made and the amount on which it is made shall be an amount equal to the excess of those moneys over the residue of expenditure.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (b)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 Notwithstanding anything in paragraph (a), in no case shall the amount on which a balancing charge is made on a person exceed the aggregate of the allowances, if any, made to him under }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 sections 33A}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0  and }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 34}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0  in respect of the expenditure in question.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i\fs22\qr\sb0\sa80\li720\sl260{{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qr\qr\li720\cf1 \f0 (Replaced }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qr\qr\li720\cf1 \f0 12 of 2004 s. 12}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qr\qr\li720\cf1 \f0 )\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs18\qj\sb0\sa0\li720{{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs18\qj\qj\li720\cf1 \f1 _____________________\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs18\qj\sb0\sa0\li720{{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs18\qj\qj\li720\cf1 \f1 Editorial Note:\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs2\qj\sb0\sa0\f