 }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (a)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 if the Commissioner is satisfied that owing to absence from Hong Kong, sickness or other reasonable cause, the person objecting to the assessment was prevented from giving such notice within such period, the Commissioner shall extend the period as may be reasonable in the circumstances;}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0  }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (Amended }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 7 of 1986 s. 12}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 )\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (b)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 where any assessment objected to has been made under }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 section 59(3)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0  in the absence of any return required under }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 section 51}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 , no notice of objection against such assessment shall be valid unless, in addition to such notice being valid in accordance with the foregoing provisions of this subsection, the return required as aforesaid has been made within the period provided by this subsection for objecting to the assessment or within such further period as the Commissioner may approve for the making of such return;\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (c)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 where the assessment is a reassessment of the tax due from a person having the effect of either increasing or reducing that person\u8217??s liability to tax, the person so reassessed shall have no further right of objection than he would have had if the reassessment had not been made except to the extent to which, by reason of the reassessment, a fresh liability in respect of any particular is imposed on him or an existing liability in respect of any particular is increased or reduced.}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0  }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (Replaced }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 2 of 1971 s. 41}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 )\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (1A)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 For the purposes of subsection (1), where a person chargeable to tax is assessed under }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 section 59(2)(b)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0  or }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 60(1)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0  in circumstances that, if the person had no other income, property or profits chargeable to tax under this Ordinance, the assessment would have been made under }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 section 59(3)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \u8212??\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (a)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 the provisions of proviso (b) to subsection (1) shall apply to any objection made against that assessment to the extent to which that person has failed to comply with }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 section 51}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 ; and\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (b)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 no notice of objection against such assessment shall be valid unless and until that person has complied with }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 section 51}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 .}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0  }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (Added }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 52 of 1993 s. 10}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 )\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (2)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 On receipt of a valid notice of objection under subsection (1) the Commissioner shall consider the same and within a reasonable time may confirm, reduce, increase or annul the assessment objected to, and for the purpose of discharging his functions under this subsection may, by notice in writing, require the person giving the notice of objection to furnish such particulars as the Commissioner may deem necessary with respect to the matters which are the subject of the assessment and to produce all books or other documents in his custody or under his control relating to such matters, and may summon any person who in his opinion is able to give evidence respecting the assessment to attend before him and may examine such person on oath or otherwise. Where the Commissioner proposes to examine any person on oath under this subsection, he shall, by prior notice in writing, afford a reasonable opportunity to the person giving the notice of objection or his authorized representative to be present at such examination. \par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (3)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 In the event of the Commissioner agreeing with any person assessed, who has validly objected to an assessment made upon him, as to the amount at which such person is liable to be assessed, any necessary adjustment of the assessment shall be made.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (4)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 In the event of the Commissioner failing to agree with any person assessed, who has validly objected to an assessment made upon him, as to the amount at which such person is liable to be assessed, the Commissioner shall, within 1 month after his determination of the objection, transmit in writing to the person objecting to the assessment his determination together with the reasons therefor and a statement of the facts upon which the determination was arrived at, and such person may appeal therefrom to the Board of Review as provided in }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 section 66}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 .\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (5)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\l