\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0  is not endorsed by the Board, the relevant appeal shall be heard by it. }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (Added }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 63 of 1997 s. 6}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 )\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (2)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 Subject to subsection (2B), an appellant shall attend at the meeting of the Board at which the appeal is heard in person or by an authorized representative. }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (Amended }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 40 of 1972 s. 8}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 )\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (2A)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (Repealed }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 63 of 1997 s. 6}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 )\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (2B)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 If, on the date fixed for the hearing of an appeal, the appellant fails to attend at the meeting of the Board either in person or by his authorized representative the Board may\u8212??\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (a)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 if satisfied that the appellant\u8217??s failure to attend was due to sickness or other reasonable cause, postpone or adjourn the hearing for such period as it thinks fit;\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (b)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 proceed to hear the appeal under subsection (2D); or\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (c)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 dismiss the appeal. }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (Added }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 40 of 1972 s. 8}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 )\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (2C)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 If an appeal has been dismissed by the Board under subsection }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (2B)(c)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0  the appellant may, within 30 days after the making of the order for dismissal by notice in writing addressed to the clerk to the Board, apply to the Board to review its order and the Board may, if satisfied that the appellant\u8217??s failure to attend at the meeting of the Board for the hearing of the appeal was due to sickness or any other reasonable cause, set aside the order for dismissal and proceed to hear the appeal. }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (Added }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 40 of 1972 s. 8}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 )\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (2D)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 The Board may, if satisfied that an appellant will be or is outside Hong Kong on the date fixed for the hearing of the appeal and is unlikely to be in Hong Kong within such period thereafter as the Board considers reasonable on the application of the appellant made by notice in writing addressed to the clerk to the Board and received by him at least 7 days prior to the date fixed for the hearing of the appeal, proceed to hear the appeal in the absence of the appellant or his authorized representative. }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (Added }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 40 of 1972 s. 8}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 . Amended }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 7 of 1986 s. 12}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 )\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (2E)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 The Board may, if it hears an appeal in the absence of an appellant or his authorized representative under subsection (2D), consider such written submissions as the appellant may submit to the Board. }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (Added }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 40 of 1972 s. 8}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 . Amended }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 7 of 1975 s. 42}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 )\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (3)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 The assessor who made the assessment appealed against or some other person authorized by the Commissioner shall attend such meeting of the Board in support of the assessment.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (4)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 The onus of proving that the assessment appealed against is excessive or incorrect shall be on the appellant. }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (Replaced }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 35 of 1965 s. 34}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 )\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (5)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 All appeals shall be heard in camera, but any appeal may be reported in such publications as may be approved by the Secretary for Justice in such a manner that the identity of the appellant is not disclosed. }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (Replaced }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 2 of 1971 s. 43}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 . Amended }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 L.N. 362 of 1997}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 )\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (6)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 The Board shall have power to summon to attend at the hearing any person whom it may consider able to give evidence respecting the appeal and may examine him as a witness either on oath or otherwise. Any person so attending may be allowed by the Board any reasonable expenses necessarily incurred by him in so attending.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (7)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 At the hearing of the appeal the Board may, subject to the provisions of }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 section 66(3)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 , admit or reject any evidence adduced, whether oral or documentary, and the provisions of the Evidence Ordinance (}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 Cap. 8}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 ), relating to the admissibility of evidence shall not apply.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1680\li1680\tqr\tx960\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (8)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (a)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 After hearing the appeal, the Board shall confirm, reduce, increase or annul the assessment appealed against or may remit the case to the Commissioner with the opinion of the Board thereon.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (b)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 Where a case is so remitted by the Board, the Commissioner shall revise the assessment as the opinion of the Board may require and in accordance with such directions (if any) as the Board, at the request at any time of the Commissioner, may give concerning the revision required in order to give effect to such opinion. }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (Replaced }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 35 of 1965 s. 34}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 )\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (9)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 Where under subsection (8), the Board does not reduce or annul such assessment, the Board may order the appellant to pay as costs of the Board a sum not exceeding the amount specified in }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 Part 1 of Schedule 5}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 , which shall be added to the tax charged and recovered therewith. }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (Amended }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 11 of 1985 s. 5}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 ; }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 56 of 1993 s. 27}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 ; }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 12 of 2004 s. 14}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 )\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (9A)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 The Secretary for Financial Services and the Treasury may by order amend the amount specified in }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 Part 1 of Schedule 5}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 . }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (Added }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 12 of 2004 s. 14}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 )\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (10)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 The Board shall for the purpose of this section have the powers granted under }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 section 4(1)(d)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 , (e), (f) and (g) of the Commissions of Inquiry Ordinance (}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 Cap. 86}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 ), subject to the provisions of }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 section 80}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0  of this Ordinance. }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (Added }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 35 of 1965 s. 34}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 . Amended }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 26 of 1969 s. 35}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 )\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (11)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 Subject to section 69, the Board\u8217??s decision on the appeal is final. }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (Added }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 17 of 2015 s. 6}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 )\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i\fs22\qr\sb0\sa80\li720\sl260{{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qr\qr\li720\cf1 \f0 (Amended }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qr\qr\li720\cf1 \f0 E.R. 1 of 2012}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qr\qr\li720\cf1 \f0 )\par }}
