\clbrdrt\brdrtbl \clbrdrl\brdrtbl \clbrdrb\brdrtbl \clbrdrr\brdrtbl\clpadl0\clpadfl3\clpadt0\clpadft3\clpadb0\clpadfb3\clpadr0\clpadfr3\clshdrawnil\cltxlrtb\clftsWidth2\clwWidth2000\clNoWrap\cellx9386\row}}}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b\i0\fs28\qc\sb240\sa80\keepn\li0\sl320{{\b\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs28\qc\qc\li0\cf1 \f0 GloBE Rules\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i\fs22\qr\sb0\sa80\li0\sl260{{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qr\qr\li0\cf1 \f0 (}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qr\qr\li0\cf1 \f0 Schedule 61}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qr\qr\li0\cf1 \f0  added }{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qr\qr\li0\cf1 \f0 21 of 2025 s. 31}{\b0\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qr\qr\li0\cf1 \f0 )\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b\i0\fs28\qc\sb240\sa80\li0\sl320{{\b\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs28\qc\qc\li0\cf1 \f0 Part 1\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs18\qj\sb0\sa80\li720\sl260{{\b\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs18\qj\qj\li720\cf1 \f0 Notes\u8212??\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs18\qj\sb0\sa0\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs18\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 1.\u160??\u160??}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs18\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs18\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 This Part adopts the OECD GloBE model rules (except Articles 2.4.2, 8.1, 8.3 and 9.4 of those rules) with certain necessary changes made.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs18\qj\sb0\sa0\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs18\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 2.\u160??\u160??}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs18\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs18\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 Notes are added, after certain Articles in this Part, to refer to the relevant specified OECD GloBE rules guidance.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs18\qj\sb0\sa0\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs18\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 3.\u160??\u160??}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs18\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs18\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 Also, notes are added, after certain Articles in this Part, to point out modifications made to those Articles by Part 2 of this Schedule.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b\i0\fs28\ql\sb240\sa80\keepn\li240\sl260{{\b\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs28\ql\ql\li240\cf1 \f0 Chapter 1 Scope\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b\i0\fs22\ql\sb240\sa80\keepn\li240\sl260{{\b\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\ql\ql\li240\cf1 \f0 Article 1.1. Scope of GloBE rules\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb240\sa80\fi-720\li720\sl260{{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li720\cf1 \f0 \u160??\u160??1.1.1.}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li720\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li720\cf1 \f0 The GloBE rules apply to constituent entities that are members of an MNE group that has annual revenue of EUR 750 million or more in the consolidated financial statements of the ultimate parent entity (UPE) in at least two of the four fiscal years immediately preceding the tested fiscal year. Further rules are set out in Article 6.1 which modify the application of the consolidated revenue threshold in certain cases.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb240\sa80\fi-720\li720\sl260{{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li720\cf1 \f0 \u160??\u160??1.1.2.}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li720\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li720\cf1 \f0 If one or more of the fiscal years of the MNE group taken into account for purposes of Article 1.1.1 is of a period other than 12 months, for each of those fiscal years the EUR 750 million threshold is adjusted proportionally to correspond with the length of the relevant fiscal year.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb240\sa80\fi-720\li720\sl260{{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li720\cf1 \f0 \u160??\u160??1.1.3.}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li720\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li720\cf1 \f0 Entities that are excluded entities are not subject to the GloBE rules.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b\i0\fs22\ql\sb240\sa80\keepn\li240\sl260{{\b\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\ql\ql\li240\cf1 \f0 Article 1.2. MNE group and group\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb240\sa80\fi-720\li720\sl260{{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li720\cf1 \f0 \u160??\u160??1.2.1.}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li720\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li720\cf1 \f0 An MNE group means any group that includes at least one entity or permanent establishment that is not located in the jurisdiction of the ultimate parent entity.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb240\sa80\fi-720\li720\sl260{{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li720\cf1 \f0 \u160??\u160??1.2.2.}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li720\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li720\cf1 \f0 A group means a collection of entities that are related through ownership or control such that the assets, liabilities, income, expenses and cash flows of those entities:\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (a)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 are included in the consolidated financial statements of the ultimate parent entity; or\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1200\tqr\tx960\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 (b)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 are excluded from the consolidated financial statements of the ultimate parent entity solely on size or materiality grounds, or on the grounds that the entity is held for sale.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb240\sa80\fi-720\li720\s