}}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (a)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 the date of distribution; and\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (b)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 the date on which the constituent entity becomes entitled to the distribution.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-480\li1200\sl260{{\b\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 Prior period errors and changes in accounting principles}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0  (}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f13\u21069??\u26399??\u37679??\u35492??\u21450??\u26371??\u35336??\u21407??\u21063??\u30340??\u35722??\u21205??}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 ) means all changes in the opening equity at the beginning of the fiscal year of a constituent entity attributable to:\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (a)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 a correction of an error in the determination of financial accounting net income in a previous fiscal year that affected the income or expenses includible in the computation of GloBE income or loss for such fiscal year, except to the extent such error correction resulted in a material decrease to a liability for covered taxes subject to Article 4.6; or\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (b)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 a change in accounting principle or policy that affects income or expenses includible in the computation of GloBE income or loss.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-480\li1200\sl260{{\b\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 Qualified ancillary international shipping income}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0  (}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f13\u21512??\u36039??\u26684??\u38468??\u24118??\u22283??\u38555??\u28023??\u36939??\u25910??\u20837??}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 ) is defined in Article 3.3.3.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-480\li1200\sl260{{\b\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 Qualified domestic minimum top-up tax}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0  (}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f13\u21512??\u36039??\u26684??\u30070??\u22320??\u26368??\u20302??\u35036??\u36275??\u31237??}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 ) means a minimum tax that is included in the domestic law of a jurisdiction and that:\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (a)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 determines the excess profits of the constituent entities located in the jurisdiction (domestic excess profits) in a manner that is equivalent to the GloBE rules;\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (b)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 operates to increase domestic tax liability with respect to domestic excess profits to the minimum rate for the jurisdiction and constituent entities for a fiscal year;\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (c)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 is implemented and administered in a way that is consistent with the outcomes provided for under the GloBE rules and the Commentary, provided that such jurisdiction does not provide any benefits that are related to such rules; and\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (d)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 has the status of a qualified domestic minimum top-up tax (including transitional qualified status) for the fiscal year as determined by the Inclusive Framework.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\li1200\sl260{{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 A qualified domestic minimum top-up tax may compute domestic excess profits based on an acceptable financial accounting standard permitted by the authorised accounting body or an authorised financial accounting standard adjusted to prevent any material competitive distortions, rather than the financial accounting standard used in the consolidated financial statements.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-480\li1200\sl260{{\b\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 Qualified IIR}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0  (}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f13\u21512??\u36039??\u26684??\u25910??\u20837??\u32013??\u20837??\u35215??\u21063??}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 ) means a set of rules equivalent to Article 2.1 to Article 2.3 of the GloBE rules (including any provisions of the GloBE rules associated with those articles) that are included in the domestic law of a jurisdiction and that are implemented and administered in a way that is consistent with the outcomes provided for under the GloBE rules and the Commentary provided that such jurisdiction does not provide any benefits that are related to such rules, and the rules have qualified status (including transitional qualified status) for the fiscal year as determined by the Inclusive Framework.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-480\li1200\sl260{{\b\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 Qualified imputation tax}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0  (}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f13\u21512??\u36039??\u26684??\u27512??\u38598??\u31237??}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 ) means a covered tax accrued or paid by a constituent entity that is refundable or creditable to the beneficial owner of a dividend distributed by such constituent entity (or, in the case of a covered tax accrued or paid by a permanent establishment, a dividend distributed by the main entity) to the extent that the refund is payable, or the credit is provided:\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (a)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 by a jurisdiction other than the jurisdiction which imposed the covered taxes under a foreign tax credit regime;\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (b)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 to a beneficial owner of the dividend that is subject to tax at a nominal rate that equals or exceeds the minimum rate on the dividend on a current basis under the domestic law of the jurisdiction which imposed the covered taxes on the constituent entity;\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (c)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 to an individual beneficial owner of the dividend who is tax resident in the jurisdiction which imposed the covered taxes on the constituent entity and who is subject to tax on the dividends as ordinary income; or\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-1080\li1680\tqr\tx1440\sl260{\tab{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 (d)}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 \tab }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1680\cf1 \f0 to a governmental entity, an international organisation, a resident non-profit organisation, a resident pension fund, a resident investment entity that is not a group entity, or a resident life insurance company to the extent that the dividends are received in connection with a pension fund business and subject to tax in a similar manner as a dividend received by pension fund.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\li1200\sl260{{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 For purposes of paragraph (d), a non-profit organisation or pension fund is resident in a jurisdiction if it is created and managed in that jurisdiction, and an investment entity is resident in a jurisdiction if it is created and regulated in the jurisdiction. A life insurance company is resident in the jurisdiction in which it is located.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-480\li1200\sl260{{\b\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 Qualified refundable tax credit}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0  (}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f13\u21512??\u36039??\u26684??\u21487??\u36864??\u36996??\u31237??\u25910??\u25269??\u20813??}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 ) means a refundable tax credit designed in a way such that it must be paid as cash or available as cash equivalents within four years from when a constituent entity satisfies the conditions for receiving the credit under the laws of the jurisdiction granting the credit. A tax credit that is refundable in part is a qualified refundable tax credit to the extent it must be paid as cash or available as cash equivalents within four years from when a constituent entity satisfies the conditions for receiving the credit under the laws of the jurisdiction granting the credit. A qualified refundable tax credit does not include any amount of tax creditable or refundable pursuant to a qualified imputation tax or a disqualified refundable imputation tax.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-480\li1200\sl260{{\b\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 Qualified UTPR}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0  (}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f13\u21512??\u36039??\u26684??\u20302??\u31237??\u21033??\u28516??\u35215??\u21063??}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 ) means a set of rules equivalent to Article 2.4 to Article 2.6 of the GloBE rules (including any provisions of the GloBE rules associated with those articles) that are included in the domestic law of a jurisdiction and that are implemented and administered in a way that is consistent with the outcomes provided for under the GloBE rules and the Commentary provided that such jurisdiction does not provide any benefits that are related to such rules, and the rules have qualified status (including transitional qualified status) for the fiscal year as determined by the Inclusive Framework.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-480\li1200\sl260{{\b\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 Qualifying competent authority agreement}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0  (}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f13\u21512??\u36039??\u26684??\u20027??\u31649??\u30070??\u23616??\u21332??\u35696??}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 ) means a bilateral or multilateral agreement or arrangement between competent authorities that provides for the automatic exchange of annual GloBE information returns.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-480\li1200\sl260{{\b\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 Real estate investment vehicle}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0  (}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f13\u25151??\u22320??\u29986??\u25237??\u36039??\u24037??\u20855??}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 ) means an entity the taxation of which achieves a single level of taxation either in its hands or the hands of its interest holders (with at most one year of deferral), provided that that person holds predominantly immovable property and is itself widely held.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs18\qj\sb0\sa80\li1200\sl260{{\b\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs18\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 Note\u8212??\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs18\qj\sb0\sa80\li1200\sl260{{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs18\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 In relation to Article 10.1.1 (definition of }{\b\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs18\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 real estate investment vehicle}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs18\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 ), see the specified OECD GloBE rules guidance in }{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs18\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0 paragraph 147}{\b0\i0\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs18\qj\qj\li1200\cf1 \f0  of Chapter 10 of the 2023 Commentary.\par }}\pard\plain\nosnaplinegrid\b0\i0\fs22\qj\sb0\sa80\fi-480\li1200\sl260{{\b\i\nosupersub\nosupersub\fs22\qj\qj\li